{{also|bara|bára|Bára|bāra}}
==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmq-osw|sv}} {{term|bæra|lang=gmq-osw}}, from {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|bera|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*beraną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sv}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*bʰére-}}, from {{term/t|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}.
Cognate with Danish {{term|bære|lang=da}} and Norwegian {{term|bære|lang=no}}. <ref>{{R:runeberg.org|svetym|0166.html bära}}</ref>

See the English verb {{term|bear|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-bära.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Verb===
{{head|sv|verb}}

# to [[carry]]; to lift and transport anywhere else
# to [[wear]]; e.g. a piece of clothing or jewelery
# (''somewhat dated'') to [[lead]] to; end up at

